From 2889764cbc0458d392d5921bb4b9cb7eb6e80486 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:20:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 29/63] ARM: SMP, timers and the NVIDIA Tegra 2

- bring up the other CPUs, keep track of the paging structures active
  on each of them, switch branch prediction on for every CPU
- route device interrupts to the CPUs the kernel assigns them to
  ("arm_spread_interrupts false" in the kernel settings keeps them on the
  boot CPU)
- a timer driver for the Cortex-A9 private timer, and the Tegra 2 timers;
  do not handle ICIs while waiting for the time
- reset and switch off NVIDIA Tegra machines through the power
  management controller (the AC100 is switched off instead of reset)

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
